## FINDINGS SUMMARY

| Question | Answer | Risk in Worktrees |
|----------|--------|-------------------|
| **1. Project-root resolution** | Upwalk from cwd, stops at first `.bth.toml` | None — same `.bth.toml` at repo root for all worktrees |
| **2. Git worktree handling** | Git commands auto-resolve `.git` file pointer; hash, branch, dirty are worktree-specific | None — correct behavior, returns per-worktree state |
| **3. Project slug** | Loaded from `.bth.toml`, shared across repo | None — same slug for all worktrees |
| **4. Catalog directory** | Default `~/.bth/catalog/`, shared global; can override with `BTH_CATALOG_DIR` or `.bth.toml` | **SHARED BY DEFAULT** — parallel writes from two worktrees may race. Cool tier is SLURM-safe but same-machine concurrency untested. |
| **5. Sidecar resolution** | Find adjacent `<stem>.bth.toml`, resolve path with `.resolve()` | None — symlink handling works correctly |
| **6. Workspace concept** | Refers to project root directory in postmortem validation; "workspace level" in export is external (Claude Code / Gemini) | None — no separate workspace abstraction in bathos |
| **7. Existing tests** | Cover upwalk, git capture, config loading, but NOT explicit worktree scenario | **Gap** — no tests from `.claude/worktrees/` |
| **8. Schema migration** | Schema v7; migrations backfill missing columns via `migrate_catalog()` | None — migration mechanism is solid |

**Critical observation:** If two worktrees write to the same catalog simultaneously, cool-tier write safety is unknown. Cool Parquet is atomic write-then-rename (SLURM-safe), but concurrent writes from the same machine have not been tested.
